    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0129" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/19747</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Chief of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pétain</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-16">January 16,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear President</hi>: I was happy to receive your
                    New Year’s message<anchor n="2" xml:id="d132-f1"/> and at the same time to have
                    confirmation of the interest which you had felt in our recent
                        conversations<anchor n="3" xml:id="d132-f2"/> with Admiral Leahy.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d132-f3"/> During the course of these conversations, French
                    policy was clearly defined both by me and by the Vice President of the
                        Council<anchor n="5" xml:id="d132-f4"/> and I see with keen satisfaction
                    that the Government of the United States understands the position of the French
                    Government in the present conflict.</p>
                <p>The sentiments which you were good enough to express to me on this occasion
                    respond to those which the French people feel for the American nation and you
                    may be assured of the fidelity of the French to the traditions which you
                    invoke.</p>
                <p>I was very much touched by the good wishes which your message brought me; I beg
                    you to find here the expression of my thanks and the renewal of my best
                    wishes.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ph. Pétain</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
